read missing -> READ_FILE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT open D\missing
    could not read D\missing: there is no such file
read directory -> READ_FILE_ERROR_WRONG_TYPE EISDIR read D\sub
    could not read D\sub: it is a folder, not a file
read through file -> READ_FILE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT open D\file.txt\x
    could not read D\file.txt\x: there is no such file
read empty path -> READ_FILE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT open 
    could not read "": there is no such file
read zero char -> READ_FILE_ERROR_PATH ERR_INVALID_PATH open a\0b
    could not read "a\0b": the path has a zero character in it
read bad name -> READ_FILE_ERROR_PATH EINVAL open D\a?b.txt
    could not read D\a?b.txt: the name has characters the system does not allow, such as ? or *
read bad number -> READ_FILE_ERROR_SYSTEM EBADF read <fd 99>
    could not read <fd 99>: it is not an open file
write missing dir -> WRITE_FILE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT open D\missing\x.txt
    could not write D\missing\x.txt: the folder D\missing does not exist; create it with mkdirSync(path, { recursive: true })
write exclusive -> WRITE_NEW_FILE_ERROR_EXISTS EEXIST open D\file.txt
    could not write D\file.txt: it already exists
write directory -> WRITE_FILE_ERROR_WRONG_TYPE EISDIR open D\sub
    could not write D\sub: it is a folder, not a file
append missing dir -> APPEND_FILE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT open D\missing\x.txt
    could not append to D\missing\x.txt: the folder D\missing does not exist; create it with mkdirSync(path, { recursive: true })
append exclusive -> APPEND_NEW_FILE_ERROR_EXISTS EEXIST open D\file.txt
    could not append to D\file.txt: it already exists
mkdir existing -> MAKE_DIRECTORY_ERROR_EXISTS EEXIST mkdir D\sub
    could not create the folder D\sub: it already exists
mkdir existing file -> MAKE_DIRECTORY_ERROR_EXISTS EEXIST mkdir D\file.txt
    could not create the folder D\file.txt: it already exists
mkdir missing parent -> MAKE_DIRECTORY_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT mkdir D\missing\a
    could not create the folder D\missing\a: the folder D\missing does not exist; pass { recursive: true } to create it too
mkdir under file -> MAKE_DIRECTORY_ERROR_WRONG_TYPE ENOTDIR mkdir D\file.txt\a\b
    could not create the folder D\file.txt\a\b: a part of the path is a file, not a folder
mkdtemp missing -> MAKE_TEMPORARY_DIRECTORY_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT mkdtemp D\missing\t-XXXXXX
    could not create a temporary folder at D\missing\t-XXXXXX: the folder D\missing does not exist
rmdir not empty -> REMOVE_DIRECTORY_ERROR_NOT_EMPTY ENOTEMPTY rmdir D\sub
    could not remove the folder D\sub: it is not empty; pass { recursive: true } to rmSync to remove it with its contents
rmdir file -> REMOVE_DIRECTORY_ERROR_WRONG_TYPE ENOTDIR rmdir D\file.txt
    could not remove the folder D\file.txt: it is a file, not a folder
rmdir missing -> REMOVE_DIRECTORY_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT rmdir D\missing
    could not remove the folder D\missing: there is no such folder
unlink directory -> UNLINK_ERROR_PERMISSION EPERM unlink D\sub
    could not remove D\sub: it is a folder; remove it with rmdirSync, or with its contents with rmSync(path, { recursive: true })
unlink missing -> UNLINK_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT unlink D\missing
    could not remove D\missing: there is no such file or folder
rm directory -> REMOVE_ERROR_WRONG_TYPE EISDIR rm D\sub
    could not remove D\sub: it is a folder; pass { recursive: true } to rmSync to remove it with its contents
rm missing -> REMOVE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT lstat D\missing
    could not remove D\missing: there is no such file or folder
rm missing recursive -> REMOVE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT lstat D\missing
    could not remove D\missing: there is no such file or folder
rm missing force -> no error
rename missing -> RENAME_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT rename D\missing
    could not move D\missing to D\x: there is no such file
rename onto file -> RENAME_ERROR_EXISTS EEXIST rename D\file.txt
    could not move D\file.txt to D\other.txt: other.txt already exists; to replace it on purpose, use replaceSync from "tz:fs"
rename onto directory -> RENAME_ERROR_EXISTS EEXIST rename D\file.txt
    could not move D\file.txt to D\sub: sub already exists; to replace it on purpose, use replaceSync from "tz:fs"
copy missing -> COPY_FILE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT copyfile D\missing
    could not copy D\missing to D\x: there is no such file
copy onto file -> COPY_FILE_ERROR_EXISTS EEXIST copyfile D\file.txt
    could not copy D\file.txt to D\other.txt: other.txt already exists; to replace it on purpose, copy to a temporary name and move that over it with replaceSync from "tz:fs"
copy directory -> COPY_FILE_ERROR_WRONG_TYPE EISDIR copyfile D\sub
    could not copy D\sub to D\x: it is a folder, not a file
copy onto itself -> COPY_FILE_ERROR_EXISTS EEXIST copyfile D\file.txt
    could not copy D\file.txt to D\file.txt: file.txt already exists; to replace it on purpose, copy to a temporary name and move that over it with replaceSync from "tz:fs"
replace missing -> REPLACE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT rename D\missing
    could not move D\missing to D\other.txt: there is no such file
replace onto folder -> REPLACE_ERROR_WRONG_TYPE EISDIR rename D\file.txt
    could not move D\file.txt to D\sub: D\sub is a folder
readdir file -> READ_DIRECTORY_ERROR_WRONG_TYPE ENOTDIR scandir D\file.txt
    could not list D\file.txt: it is a file, not a folder
readdir missing -> READ_DIRECTORY_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT scandir D\missing
    could not list D\missing: there is no such folder
stat missing -> STATUS_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT stat D\missing
    could not get the info of D\missing: there is no such file or folder
stat missing, no throw -> no error
lstat missing -> LINK_STATUS_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT lstat D\missing
    could not get the info of D\missing: there is no such file or folder
stat through file -> STATUS_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT stat D\file.txt\x
    could not get the info of D\file.txt\x: there is no such file or folder
realpath missing -> REAL_PATH_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT lstat D\missing
    could not resolve D\missing: there is no such file or folder
access missing -> ACCESS_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT access D\missing
    could not check D\missing: there is no such file or folder
chmod missing -> CHANGE_MODE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT chmod D\missing
    could not change the mode of D\missing: there is no such file or folder
truncate missing -> TRUNCATE_ERROR_NOT_FOUND ENOENT open D\missing
    could not truncate D\missing: there is no such file
false false
dest: D\other.txt
replace onto file -> no error
false text
false
